# shadcn/ui + React Aria

Use shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui/*` for any interactive or accessible UI primitive. This project uses the `aria-nova` style on top of `react-aria-components`.

## Required

- **New components**: Prefer shadcn/ui. Add missing primitives with `npx shadcn@latest add <component>`.
- **Touched components**: When editing existing UI, replace hand-rolled primitives in that file with shadcn/ui equivalents in the same change.
- **Imports**: `@/components/ui/button`, `@/components/ui/dropdown-menu`, `@/components/ui/tabs`, etc.

## Use shadcn/ui for

- Buttons and button-styled links → `Button`, `LinkButton`
- Menus and popovers → `DropdownMenu*`
- Tabs → `Tabs`, `TabsList`, `TabsTrigger`
- Form controls → `Input`, `Select`, etc.
- Feedback → `Alert`, `Badge`
- Layout shells with design-system semantics → `Card`, `Separator`

## Colors and styling

Use shadcn semantic Tailwind classes only — no custom theme tokens or hex colors in components.

**Default: omit color classes.** `body` sets `bg-background text-foreground`; shadcn components (`Card`, `Button`, `Alert`, `Badge`, …) ship their own colors. Only add a color utility when the element must differ from its parent:

- De-emphasized copy (hints, labels, metadata, footer) → `text-muted-foreground`
- Brand emphasis or links → `text-primary`
- Errors → `text-destructive`, `Alert variant="destructive"`
- Interactive state styling on toggles, selected chips, etc.

Do not repeat `text-foreground`, `bg-background`, `bg-card`, or `border-border` when inheritance or the component default already provides them.

Do not use legacy app tokens (`text-accent`, `text-muted`, `bg-surface`, `bg-chip`, `text-success`, etc.).

## Keep custom only when

- No shadcn primitive exists and adding one is out of scope for the change
- Pure layout/composition wrappers with no interaction semantics (e.g. section headings)
- Static semantic markup (e.g. footer copyright text)

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ Hand-rolled menu with manual focus/escape handling
<button onClick={() => setOpen(!open)} aria-haspopup="menu">...</button>
{open ? <div role="menu">...</div> : null}

// ✅ shadcn/ui dropdown
<DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <Button aria-label="Account menu">...</Button>
  <DropdownMenu>...</DropdownMenu>
</DropdownMenuTrigger>
```

```tsx
// ❌ Styled native button for navigation
<button className="border-b-2 ..." onClick={() => router.push(...)}>

// ✅ shadcn/ui tabs
<Tabs selectedKey={id} onSelectionChange={(key) => router.push(...)}>
  <TabsList variant="line">...</TabsList>
</Tabs>
```

Reference implementations: `components/site-header.tsx`, `components/jargon/profile-menu.tsx`, `components/jargon/collection-tabs.tsx`.
